{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106555-djinns-as-familiars","id":1106555,"title":"Djinns as familiars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-22T08:08:36-07:00","id":1106555,"title":"Djinns as familiars","content":"So, can one have a djinn as a familiar...? How could it be done? Do you give it Charms like a spirit or you give him Arete and some Spheres to allow it to cast spells?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because it would be fun to have one for a mage, but not sure how it could happen. Would they cost like 5 dots in the background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:04:07-07:00","id":1106590,"title":"","content":"Certainly you can. A djinn Familiar is far from the strangest thing Mage permits as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Familiars, by their nature, are not Awakened beings. If you wanted an Awakened creature to be your best bud, take multiple dots in Ally to reflect that (because a character with Spheres is inherently more potent than a common, mundane Ally; as are vampires, werewolves, changelings, wraiths, etc.). But more importantly, I don't think Djinn can be Awakened. They are spiritual beings, who live predominantly in the Umbra. So no, you wouldn't give a Djinn Spheres; they would have Charms just like any other Umbrood.<br /> <br /> The background cost for a Familiar indicates how many freebie points they distribute at character creation (10 x background rating). These are used to buy Attribute and Ability dots and the like, as well as spirit-specific traits like Charms and Essence. Seen in this light, a Djinn Familiar is as powerful as you want to make them, given how many background and (the mage's) freebie points you want to invest in them. All of these rules get detailed in the Revised edition book, <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:20:39-07:00","id":1107818,"title":"","content":"Apparently in Dark Ages, Djinni rhetoric about how special and unique and powerful they are compared to other spirits make a lot more sense and they DO have sphere ratings and arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:39:17-07:00","id":1108108,"title":"","content":"<b> Lost Paths </b> includes an entire chapter on the Djinn. It allows them as Familiars, but notes that you can only get that level of friendship and cooperation from a Djinn if you get it to willingly agree to the bargain. As well, the Djinn are described as having Charms, not Arete or Spheres (although the wish-granting Charm has versatility reminiscent of Spheres). As far as I can tell, the business about the Djinn being Awakened is a bit of fanon, with no published support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:26:09-07:00","id":1108125,"title":"","content":"Lost Paths isn't very clear about that. In the Taftani section they say that Genies are sometimes held as Familiars, even that it's common for them to grant such to their apprentices...and in the Genie section they say that genies would NEVER become Familiars (maybe they meant that genie only will become familiars if they're magically forced to do so?). Anycase it's true that there genies don't have Spheres in that book (and probably genies able to use the Wish charm are too powerful to be taken as familiars anyway).<br /> <br /> However, in DA: Mage Grimoire you have a small section with genies, and they DO have Pillars...soo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T01:28:38-07:00","id":1139856,"title":"","content":"I think Dark Age Mage in general has more awakened entities. It also lists true dragons as being awakened beings. Dark Age Fae basically have pillars so they might as well be awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T03:22:01-07:00","id":1139864,"title":"","content":"Mage has some non-human (non-construct/non-human-soul...) entities listed with Spheres and Arete for the very same reason that Vampire often uses Discipline ratings for non-Vampire splats and creatures:<br /> Simplification and generalization. Just like the non-Vampire splats in the Vampire books don't *literally* have Vampire Disciplines, the umbrood and spirits and Djinn with specified Spheres don't actually have Spheres and Arete - but their powers tend to be versatile and flexible, so that a Sphere representation works well to make things simpler.<br /> <br /> Note that this mostly happens in older 1nd Ed/2nd Ed. mage books - I can't think of any in the Revised or M20 lineup that actually use Spheres for non-Mage entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T07:05:13-07:00","id":1139905,"title":"","content":"Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, Spheres have been used to represent other Splats, however, Spirits have always used Charms, and when their powers were vast, Charms AND Spheres. This implies a difference between having &quot;Static Charms&quot; (that are not unlike Disciplines) and, let's say, &quot;Dynamic Charms&quot; that allow to reshape reality at will. These &quot;Dynamic Charms&quot; aren't True Magick, but they use the same mechanic, and, more importantly, they're INTENDED to use the same mechanic, they aren't just a simplification of &quot;has a lot of Charms&quot;, when 1nd Ed/2nd Ed wanted to make that simplification, it just did (like with the Death Ephipling, &quot;it has any charm the ST deems appropiate&quot;). In my opinion, spirits with spheres implies someting akin to Nexus Crawler reality warping-this is NOT the same as a simplification of Disciplines.<br /> <br /> M20 allows to use Spheres to represent powerful spirits, and, as has been stated, DA (fairly modern suplement), does something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T07:22:15-07:00","id":1139915,"title":"","content":"And speaking of, I think the most Sphere'd out spirit still remains 'Abbi-Il-Aeon' from the first Book of Madness. Almost all Spheres at 5. Strength 9, Dex 10, Stamina 10, all other traits at....25. When materialized.<br /> When not, &quot;His spirit traits are too high to create&quot;. Page 128. He's quite a treat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T15:45:38-07:00","id":1140665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106555-djinns-as-familiars?p=1139864#post1139864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has some non-human (non-construct/non-human-soul...) entities listed with Spheres and Arete for the very same reason that Vampire often uses Discipline ratings for non-Vampire splats and creatures:<br /> Simplification and generalization. Just like the non-Vampire splats in the Vampire books don't *literally* have Vampire Disciplines, the umbrood and spirits and Djinn with specified Spheres don't actually have Spheres and Arete - but their powers tend to be versatile and flexible, so that a Sphere representation works well to make things simpler.<br /> <br /> Note that this mostly happens in older 1nd Ed/2nd Ed. mage books - I can't think of any in the Revised or M20 lineup that actually use Spheres for non-Mage entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>As said, it was more so a translation issue for 1st/2nd than for later editions. DA, and translated/transferred aspects, made a clear point of including for djinn that they had *both* Charms/Spirit stats and abilities as well as Arete/Foundation and Spheres/Pillars. (In goes inline with the albeit very last-minute-postings before everything went dark for the &quot;classic&quot; era in 2004 that humans, dragons (true dragons, vs. other beings that were thought of/referred to as dragons) and djinn (isfritt, by whatever name) were the known entities who could Awaken(tm), properly, and had the power of True Magic(k)(tm)... though humans who Awakened apparently did so to a greater potential and versatility than their still-often-more-powerful djinn/dragon counterparts.<br /> <br /> But at this point that is likely just rehashing old leftovers. M20 and onwards will no doubt eventually get around to re-addressing all of that in a later edition/revision... as is often the case... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:11:51-07:00","id":1142300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106555-djinns-as-familiars?p=1106590#post1106590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly you can. A djinn Familiar is far from the strangest thing Mage permits as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Familiars, by their nature, are not Awakened beings. If you wanted an Awakened creature to be your best bud, take multiple dots in Ally to reflect that (because a character with Spheres is inherently more potent than a common, mundane Ally; as are vampires, werewolves, changelings, wraiths, etc.). But more importantly, I don't think Djinn can be Awakened. They are spiritual beings, who live predominantly in the Umbra. So no, you wouldn't give a Djinn Spheres; they would have Charms just like any other Umbrood.<br /> <br /> The background cost for a Familiar indicates how many freebie points they distribute at character creation (10 x background rating). These are used to buy Attribute and Ability dots and the like, as well as spirit-specific traits like Charms and Essence. Seen in this light, a Djinn Familiar is as powerful as you want to make them, given how many background and (the mage's) freebie points you want to invest in them. All of these rules get detailed in the Revised edition book, <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be mistaken, but Familiars are freely following the Mage. It's a bond made upon trust, not coercion. Djinns are mostly compelled to obey the Mage's orders (even in Aladdin, the Djinn just wants to be free). Thus, I think Fetishes are better for Djinns (The Genie's lamp and so on). Well better does not mean necessary of course. Familiars are just fine too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T15:27:44-07:00","id":1142319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106555-djinns-as-familiars?p=1142300#post1142300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be mistaken, but Familiars are freely following the Mage. It's a bond made upon trust, not coercion. Djinns are mostly compelled to obey the Mage's orders (even in Aladdin, the Djinn just wants to be free). Thus, I think Fetishes are better for Djinns (The Genie's lamp and so on). Well better does not mean necessary of course. Familiars are just fine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all, Fetishes can be obtained through the Mage getting the spirit to inhabit the item willingly. Second, Djinn are often coerced or forced, but they don't have to be. They are rational spiritual actors, and can be bargained with just like any other Umbrood. More readily, actually, since all Djinn are sapient by default. Lost Paths even has rules for when a mage wants to do the non-standard thing, and gain the services of a Djinn through respect and bargaining, rather than by invoking the Solomonic Code.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}